title: 'Decided: a view says whose overrides it follows only when it follows the user''s.'
pid: aba644bc-91c7-4d6d-81b2-bf521648b482
body: |2-
  Following the root's author, nothing is drawn: a substituted node
  already carries its home skgrepo's herald and the overridesHere mark,
  which together say whose version it is, and the root's own herald
  says whose view it is. Once a switch exists, though, a buffer can be
  in either state with the same root, and the heralds no longer tell
  which; so a switched buffer says so where it costs nothing to the
  text: in Emacs the mode name reads "SKG:your overrides"; Neovim's
  client draws no statusline, so it keeps 'b:skg_overrides_followed'
  and offers a function for one; skg-for-ai's compact summary says it;
  and each switch says in a message what the buffer now shows. The default stays unmarked, because a mark on every view would
  say nothing.
  Unsure: under the default, one's own fork, invisible there, still
  says nothing at all.
